# Release a snap to a store channel
Publish a tested snap revision to a channel for end users.

## 1. Confirm credentials and store
Check you are logged in with the correct credentials:

  idiot env auth status

If publishing to a Dedicated Snap Store, confirm the store is set:

  idiot env store status

Switch if needed: eval "$(idiot env store use <store-name>)"

## 2. Identify the revision to release
List recent revisions and their current channels:

  snapcraft list-revisions <snap-name>

Note the revision number you want to promote.

## 3. Review the snap's current channel map
  snapcraft status <snap-name>

Understand what is currently in each channel before you change anything.

## 4. Run sanity checks on the revision
If you haven't done so, install the revision from the candidate channel and
run your integration test suite. See: idiot process show snap-install-test

## 5. Release the revision
  snapcraft release <snap-name> <revision> <channel>

Example: snapcraft release mysnap 42 stable

## 6. Confirm the release
  snapcraft status <snap-name>

Verify the revision now appears in the target channel.

## 7. Notify stakeholders
Communicate the release to customers / internal teams as needed.
Update any tracking tickets or to-do lists:

  idiot todo show <project>
